            "width": 37.98882681564246,
            "height": 8.830022075055187,
            "action": {
              "library": "H5P.AdvancedText 1.1",
              "params": {
                "text": "<p><span style=\"font-size:1.5em;\"><strong>INFORMATION TEXT (Part 2)</strong></span></p>\n"
              },
              "metadata": {
                "contentType": "Text",
                "license": "U",
                "title": "Unbenannt: Text",
                "defaultLanguage": "en"
              },
              "subContentId": "55aaf4d3-f7e3-4a3e-9196-01a6f7474f94"
            },
            "alwaysDisplayComments": false,
            "backgroundOpacity": 0,
            "displayAsButton": false,
            "buttonSize": "big",
            "goToSlideType": "specified",
            "invisible": false,
            "solution": ""
          },
          {
            "x": 2.23463687150838,
            "y": 13.245033112582782,
            "width": 92.73743016759778,
            "height": 86.09271523178808,
            "action": {
              "library": "H5P.AdvancedText 1.1",
              "params": {
                "text": "<p><strong>Leadership in the Kenya African National Union</strong><br>\nAfter his release, Kenyatta became president of the Kenya African National Union (KANU). He worked tirelessly for Kenya's independence, which was achieved on December 12, 1963. Kenyatta's leadership was crucial in the peaceful transition from colonial rule to sovereignty.</p>\n\n<p><strong>First President of Kenya</strong><br>\nJomo Kenyatta became Kenya's first president in 1964. As president, he pursued policies to unite the country's diverse ethnic groups and develop the economy. He adopted a pro-Western, anti-communist stance, aligning Kenya with the United States and Britain during the Cold War.</p>\n\n<p><strong>Economic Policies and \"Harambee\"</strong><br>\nKenyatta launched the \"Harambee\" (meaning \"all pull together\" in Swahili) campaign to encourage economic self-reliance. He promoted agriculture and industry to reduce dependence on foreign aid. His policies helped to stabilize the young nation's economy.</p>\n"
              },
              "metadata": {
                "contentType": "Text",
                "license": "U",
                "title": "Unbenannt: Text",
                "defaultLanguage": "en"
              },
              "subContentId": "3b13867b-feab-4e2e-bfa2-fcc82e4dbff1"
            },
