          {
            "x": 2.178649237472767,
            "y": 12.910611231371064,
            "width": 92.73743016759778,
            "height": 86.09271523178808,
            "action": {
              "library": "H5P.AdvancedText 1.1",
              "params": {
                "text": "<p><strong>Land Reform Under Kenyatta</strong><br>\nLand reform was a significant issue for Kenyatta. He implemented programs to redistribute land from British colonial holdings to Kenyan families. However, this process faced criticism for favoring the Kikuyu ethnic group, to which he belonged, and creating an elite class.</p>\n\n<p><strong>Cultural Impact and Legacy</strong><br>\nKenyatta is remembered for promoting African culture and heritage. He often wore traditional attire and emphasized the importance of family and cultural traditions. His legacy includes fostering a sense of national identity among Kenyans.</p>\n\n<p><strong>Controversies and Criticisms</strong><br>\nDespite his achievements, Kenyatta's presidency was not without controversy. He was criticized for developing a strong central government with authoritarian tendencies. His later years in office were marked by accusations of corruption and nepotism, which have affected views of his leadership.</p>\n"
              },
              "metadata": {
                "contentType": "Text",
                "license": "U",
                "title": "Unbenannt: Text",
